course: dictionary
lesson: 14169
title: Modesty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Modesty means not boasting about yourself or your skills, even when you are good at something. A modest person does not show off. «Mia scored the winning goal, but she just said, "The whole team did well."» Mia is good at football, but she does not boast about it, so she shows modesty.
explain: Modesty can also mean being small or not much, like a home that is simple and plain. «The family had very little money, but they lived with modesty in a small, plain house.» Here modesty does not mean a bad thing. It means the home is simple, not grand.
explain: Look out for false modesty. This is when someone pretends to be humble so that people will praise them. «Sam said, "Oh, I'm rubbish at football," so that everyone would tell him he was brilliant.» Sam is not really being modest. He wants praise, so this is false modesty.
fact: Modesty means not boasting about yourself, even when you are good at something.
fact: «Modesty» can also mean being small or not much, as in «the modesty of their home».
fact: Many faiths and cultures teach modesty in clothes: dressing in a way that does not draw attention to your body.
fact: The opposites of modesty are boastfulness, vanity and arrogance.
fact: «False modesty» means pretending to be humble to get praise.
exercise: «Mia scored the winning goal, but she said, "The whole team did well."» What does this show? | *Modesty, because she did not boast about herself | Being very loud | Anger | Boasting
exercise: Sam says, "I'm rubbish at football," so that everyone will tell him he is brilliant. What is this called? | *False modesty | Vanity | Honesty | Bravery
exercise: «The family had very little money, but they lived with modesty in a small, plain house.» What does modesty mean here? | Being sad all the time | *Being small or not much | Being very rich | Being loud in front of guests
test: Why is modesty seen as a good quality in stories and PSHE lessons? | It means you never win anything | It means you should never try your best | *It stops people showing off, so others can shine too | It means you must always shout about your wins
test: Which phrase means pretending to be humble to get praise? | Good manners | Bragging rights | True modesty | *False modesty
exam: Which sentence shows modesty? | *Ben got an A on his test and said his friends helped him a lot | Nobody else could ever do what I do | Look at my amazing new bike, nobody has one like it | I am the best at maths in the whole school
